Atomistic two-chain LJ convergence study
=========================================

Configuration
  N=(20, 40, 80, 160, 320, 640); continuum points=(400, 800)
  atomistic cutoff M=80; tail check M=160
  effective LJ: a=1, sigma=0.9, L=1, epsilon=0.5; W=4 sum V
  starts=sampled_continuum, random_fourier_seed_3; seed=3; modes=1-5; decay=1/k^2; amplitude=0.1
  acceptance: successful finite solve, Appendix B bounds, gradient <= 5.0e-08, EL_inf/h <= 1.0e-02, no resolved negative raw curvature
  gradients and EL are checked before and after normalization
  directional-gradient diagnostic step=1.00e-06
  one L-BFGS-B call; at most one conditional positive-spectrum Newton correction
  Newton step <= 0.1h; energy allowance = 64*eps*max(1, |E_before|, |E_after|)
  tau_H = max(1.0e-08, 100*eps*max(1, ||H||_inf) + 10*eigenpair residual)
  tau_E = 1.0e-10*max(1, |E_warm|, |E_seed3|)

